# Case Page Rules

- Start each case with concise context: object type, problem, outcome.
- Keep before/after media comparison prominent and easy to understand.
- Place measurable results near the top (time saved, budget impact, quality gain).
- Use clear anchors for long pages (overview, process, media, reviews, CTA).
- Keep expert video blocks optional and non-blocking for page performance.
- End with strong next step CTA to inquiry/contact.

## Media Quality

- Preserve consistent aspect ratios in galleries.
- Provide alt text that describes scene context, not only filenames.
- Avoid autoplay with sound and avoid layout jumps while media loads.
